Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook is written with Mathematica version 13.2 and is provided as a \
companion resource for readers of",
 StyleBox[" Algebraic Functions",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " by Dominic Milioto.  Commercial use of this notebook or its contents \
outside the context of the book is not permitted without the author\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s permission.\n\nThe companion Mathematica notebooks were \
developed under Mathematica 13.2 on Windows.   All file and directory \
references have been written using platform\:2011independent Wolfram Language \
functions such as FileNameJoin and NotebookDirectory[], ensuring full cross\
\:2011platform compatibility. Any current version of Mathematica on Windows, \
macOS, or Linux should run the notebooks without modification.\n\nThe 12 \
chapter notebooks are mostly interconnected, with later notebooks relying on \
data computed by earlier chapters.  Until a reader has become familiar with \
both the book and Mathematica notebooks, the simplest approach when reviewing \
the chapter tutorials is to go back as needed to the  chapter 2 notebook, \
creating annular tables, computing monodromies,  annular and central branch \
plots, then the chapter 3 notebook to compute 500-term power expansions at \
singular points needed by the chapter 4 and 5 notebooks,  then using chapter \
6 to compute 200 or more terms of high precision annular power expansions of \
a selected annular branch, which are next needed by the chapter 7 and 8 \
notebooks, and proceeding to later chapters  in sequential order until the \
chapter with the current tutorial is encountered.  For example, the chapter 6 \
tutorial begins with testCase0007.  And even though this chapter is concerned \
with annular power expansions, the reader will best understand the concepts \
of this book by first running the chapter 2 notebook, selecting testCase0007 \
and following the chapter 2 tutorial, then proceeding with the chapter 3 \
notebook and continuing the notebooks sequentially until reaching the chapter \
6 notebook.   "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
